Subject: [PATCH] swayimg: accept Meson 1.0 option-file naming

The current iOS build container ships Meson 1.0.1. swayimg 5.4 does not use
Meson 1.1-only constructs for the reduced iOS feature set, but upstream stores
project options in the Meson 1.1 `meson.options` filename. Keep that file for
new Meson and add the older `meson_options.txt` name so Meson 1.0 sees the
same options instead of rejecting every `-D...` argument as unknown.

diff -ruN -U0 --exclude=*.bak a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build	2026-06-20 22:41:12
+++ b/meson.build	2026-07-06 00:00:00
@@ -14 +14 @@
-    meson_version: '>=1.1',
+    meson_version: '>=1.0',
diff -ruN -U0 --exclude=*.bak a/meson_options.txt b/meson_options.txt
--- a/meson_options.txt	1970-01-01 00:00:00
+++ b/meson_options.txt	2026-07-06 00:00:00
@@ -0,0 +1,161 @@
